# Project 4 — Insight Discovery through EDA

## Objective
The objective of this project is to perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on the cleaned Telco Customer Churn dataset to identify important trends, patterns, risks, and opportunities related to customer churn.
The analysis focuses on converting numerical and categorical patterns into meaningful business insights.

## Business Problem
Customer churn is an important business problem for telecom companies because losing existing customers can reduce recurring revenue and increase customer acquisition costs.
This project analyzes customer characteristics and service-related factors to understand which customer groups show different churn patterns.

## Analysis Performed
### 1. Overall Churn Distribution
The distribution of customers who churned and did not churn is analyzed to understand the overall churn situation.

### 2. Churn by Contract Type
Customer churn is compared across:
* Month-to-month
* One year
* Two year
This helps identify whether contract duration is associated with different churn behaviour.

### 3. Churn by Internet Service
Churn patterns are compared across different internet service categories.

### 4. Tenure Analysis
Customer tenure is compared between churned and non-churned customers to understand whether customer lifetime is related to churn.

### 5. Monthly Charges Analysis
Monthly charges are compared between churned and non-churned customers.

### 6. Payment Method Analysis
Churn rates are compared across different payment methods.

## Visualizations
The Python script generates visualizations including:
